From 34ce4d000dd965e13531807be4570f268a3fedc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:51:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 214/273] Part: 2D export keeps the model's groups (PPTX group
 shapes, SVG <g>, JSON paths)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Field feedback on a 2,113-part truck loading model: the 28,011 shapes came
out flat on the slide.  Now every visible object is a group of its face
shapes, nested in groups for the model's hierarchy:

  PPTX  <p:grpSp> per group, frames (off/ext = chOff/chExt) are the union
        of the children, so PowerPoint shows and moves them right
  SVG   nested <g id="gN" inkscape:label="...">
  JSON  "items": [{object, label, group: [labels], groupId: [ids]}], and
        "group" on every face and edge

Where the path comes from, first match wins:
1. "group" of a dict item: "はしごの列/はしご1/間口3" or a list
2. group= argument: a function obj -> path or a dict {Name|Label|index: path}
3. a string property named "Group" on the object
4. the document tree: App::Part, document groups, App::Link (a link to an
   assembly is expanded and drawn as its own group), link arrays, a hidden
   Part::Compound whose children are drawn
Groups are identified by objects and link paths, never by labels, so
FreeCAD's renamed duplicates (間口1 -> 間口001) do not merge or split
groups.  group=False gives the flat output as before.

Collecting the scene now walks the document tree (getSubObjects): objects
in hidden App::Parts are no longer drawn, and link arrays are no longer
drawn twice (array and its elements).

Tests: rack document (nested App::Parts, renamed labels, group, link,
"Group" property, hidden object) checked in PPTX (nesting and every group
frame), SVG and JSON; dict paths and the group= argument.  1,800 boxes in
4-level App::Parts: 3,467 shapes in 1,429 groups in 3.0 s, read back with
python-pptx: all group frames equal the union of their children.

